course: dictionary
lesson: 9218
title: Solvent: the liquid that dissolves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A solvent is a liquid that dissolves other things. When you stir sugar into a cup of tea, the sugar seems to vanish. The tea is the solvent, and the sugar is the substance that gets dissolved.
explain: «Water dissolves more substances than almost any other liquid, because its molecules have slightly charged ends that pull particles apart; that is why it is called the universal solvent.» Here the clue is the word dissolves: a solvent is the thing doing the dissolving.
explain: Solvent has another meaning too. Paint thinner, glue remover and nail-varnish remover are chemical solvents, and they are strong and dangerous. Use them in fresh air, keep them away from flames, and never sniff them.
fact: A solvent is a liquid that dissolves another substance.
fact: In a solution, the solvent does the dissolving and the solute is what gets dissolved.
fact: In salt water, the salt is the solute and the water is the solvent.
fact: Water is the most common solvent, so it is called the universal solvent.
fact: Chemical solvents such as white spirit have strong fumes that are harmful to breathe, so never sniff them.
exercise: In salt water, which substance is the solvent? | *Water | Salt | Sugar | Sand
exercise: What does a chemical solvent such as white spirit do? | Makes you sleepy | Keeps food cold | *Dissolves paint, glue or grease | Makes paint shiny
exercise: «Water dissolves more substances than almost any other liquid.» Why is water called the universal solvent? | It is always cold | It never changes into steam | *It dissolves so many different substances | It is the only liquid on Earth
test: In a sugar and water drink, what is the solute? | Water | *Sugar | The spoon | The cup
test: Why should you use chemical solvents in fresh air? | To make them smell nice | *Their fumes can be harmful to breathe | So they cool down | To help them freeze
exam: In «The company is still solvent», what does solvent mean? | Dissolves paint | *Has enough money to pay its debts | Full of salt water | Very dirty
